IMPORT prelude

-- Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Cth) -- who is an employee (s 12), what counts as qualifying earnings
-- (s 10A(1)-(3) and "ordinary time earnings" in s 6(1)), the maximum contributions base as a cap (s 10A(6)), the individual
-- superannuation guarantee amount and the charge percentage (ss 17A, 17B), when an eligible contribution must be received
-- (s 18C(1), (2) item 1, "usual period", "extended usual period" and "business day" in s 6(1)), the individual base and final
-- shortfalls (ss 18C, 18D), the administrative uplift (s 19B), the choice loading and its limit (ss 20A, 20C, 20D), the
-- superannuation guarantee shortfall (s 16B), and where a contribution must go to comply with the choice of fund requirements
-- (ss 32C(1), (1A), (1B), (2), (2A), 32CA).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 78, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 57, 2025, the Treasury Laws
-- Amendment (Payday Superannuation) Act 2025), register id C2026C00272, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04402.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0012 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 6 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios: Chloe c020 (2018-03-14, turns 15, a TFN and a casual supermarket job: is super
-- payable? -- the scenario cites s 28, under 18 only if more than 30 hours a week), c032 (2023-11-20, an internship at $25 an
-- hour: is an intern an employee, is super payable? -- s 12), c041 (2024-02-29, first payslip at $5,833.33 a month: how much
-- super and where does it go? -- ss 16, 19, 23); Jake k041 (2027-03-31, delivery-platform contractor: is super payable for a
-- contractor? -- s 12(3)), k060 (2034-02-01, a security officer's award job at Sentinel -- s 16); Daniel d044 (2031-06-01,
-- Jarrah's first three employees: what does an employer owe from day one? -- ss 16, 19). SCOPED to the provisions those events
-- name as they read in this edition, with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- THIS EDITION IS THE PAYDAY SUPER TEXT. The endnotes record ss 11, 23, 27 and 28 as "rep No 57, 2025" and s 19 as "rs No 57,
-- 2025", commencing 1 July 2026. The quarterly scheme, the under-18 / 30-hour rule the scenario cites for c020, the quarterly
-- minimum the scenario cites for c041, and the 11% and 11.5% steps for 2023-24 and 2024-25 are not in the deposited text. The
-- application and transitional items of Act No. 57, 2025 are not in the compilation. INFERENCE: the repealed text still governs
-- the 2018, 2023 and 2024 events; it was not deposited, so this encoding answers those events only where the provision is
-- unchanged (s 12: last amended 2006 by the endnotes) or says plainly that it cannot.
--
-- FORMULAS NOT IN THE DEPOSIT. The formulas in ss 10A(5), 17A(2), 18A(3), 18C(1), 18D(2) and 19A(2) were images and did not
-- survive conversion: the deposit has "equal to:" and then "where:". The forms used below for 17A(2), 18C(1) and 18D(2) are
-- INFERENCES from the surrounding words (s 17: "equal to a particular percentage of the payment"; s 18C(1)(d) and s 18D(2)(d):
-- contributions applied so as not to make the result "less than nil"). The maximum contributions base (s 10A(5)) and the
-- individual notional earnings component (s 19A) are INPUTS.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Anything the regulations prescribe -- in particular any kind of employee, work or payment excluded from
-- qualifying earnings under s 10A(3)(b), an INPUT; the basic concessional contributions cap and the maximum contributions base
-- (INPUTS); the general interest charge rate and the notional earnings component (s 19A, an INPUT); reductions of the uplift by
-- regulation (s 19B(2), (3)); public holidays (an INPUT list -- s 6(1) "business day" counts a holiday "for the whole of" any
-- State, the ACT or the NT); out-of-cycle earnings and exceptional circumstances (s 18C(2) items 2-4, (3), (4)); defined benefit
-- schemes and benefit certificates (ss 6A, 6B, 10, 18A(3), 20A(3), 20B); the complying-fund presumption and its exceptions
-- (ss 18A(2), 18B); exemption certificates beyond their effect (ss 17C, 17D); the Commonwealth as employer (s 5); international
-- agreements (s 15C); anti-avoidance (s 30); the choice of fund requirements beyond s 32C(1)-(2A) and s 32CA (successor funds,
-- CSS, PSS, agreements and awards, temporary visa holders, standard choice forms); assessments, collection, the s 59C penalty,
-- payments to employees (Part 8), and records (s 79). The charge itself is imposed by the Superannuation Guarantee Charge Act
-- 1992, which was not read.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. Taking 10000 away gives the same day a year earlier (29 February is not modelled).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 -- the guarantee`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below nil` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `a`

§§ `s 12 -- employee, employer`

-- s 12(1): "employee and employer have their ordinary meaning. However, ... subsections (2) to (11): (a) expand the meaning of
-- those terms; and (b) make particular provision to avoid doubt". (2) a person "entitled to payment for the performance of duties
-- as a member of the executive body ... of a body corporate is, in relation to those duties, an employee". (3) "If a person works
-- under a contract that is wholly or principally for the labour of the person, the person is an employee of the other party to
-- the contract." (4)-(7) members of Parliament and of the Territory Legislative Assemblies. (8)(a), (b) a person "paid to perform
-- or present ... any music, play, dance, entertainment, sport, display or promotional activity", or to provide services in
-- connection with it; (c) film, tape, disc, television or radio. (9) an office holder or person "otherwise in the service of the
-- Commonwealth, of a State or of a Territory", but not "as a member of a local government council". (9A) "Subject to subsection
-- (10), a person who holds office as a member of a local government council is not an employee of the council." (10) unless
-- covered by s 12-45(1)(e) in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953. (11) "A person who is paid to do work wholly or
-- principally of a domestic or private nature for not more than 30 hours per week is not regarded as an employee in relation to
-- that work."
--
-- Nothing in s 12 asks the worker's age, whether the work is casual, or whether the worker holds an ABN. Whether a contract is
-- "wholly or principally" for labour is a judgement the Act does not define: an INPUT.
DECLARE Engagement HAS
    `an employee in the ordinary meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works under a contract wholly or principally for their labour` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid as a member of the executive body of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of a Parliament or a Territory Legislative Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid to perform or present entertainment, sport or promotion, or for services in connection with it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid for work on a film, tape, disc or broadcast` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a public office or is otherwise in government service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of a local government council in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `covered by s 12-45(1)(e) of Schedule 1 to the TAA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid for work wholly or principally domestic or private` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours a week of that work` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the engagement` IS AN Engagement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker is an employee for the Act` IF
    IF      `the engagement`'s `paid for work wholly or principally domestic or private`
        AND `the engagement`'s `hours a week of that work` AT MOST 30
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF `the engagement`'s `a member of a local government council in that capacity`
         THEN `the engagement`'s `covered by s 12-45(1)(e) of Schedule 1 to the TAA`
         ELSE     `the engagement`'s `an employee in the ordinary meaning`
              OR  `the engagement`'s `works under a contract wholly or principally for their labour`
              OR  `the engagement`'s `paid as a member of the executive body of a body corporate`
              OR  `the engagement`'s `a member of a Parliament or a Territory Legislative Assembly`
              OR  `the engagement`'s `paid to perform or present entertainment, sport or promotion, or for services in connection with it`
              OR  `the engagement`'s `paid for work on a film, tape, disc or broadcast`
              OR  `the engagement`'s `holds a public office or is otherwise in government service`

§§ `s 10A(1)-(3) and s 6(1) -- qualifying earnings`

-- s 6(1): "ordinary time earnings, for a person, means all of the person's earnings as an employee made up of: (a) earnings in
-- respect of ordinary hours of work; and (b) earnings consisting of over-award payments, shift-loading or commission; other than a
-- lump sum payment of any of the following kinds made to the person on the termination of the person's employment: (c) a payment
-- in lieu of unused sick leave; (d) an unused annual leave payment, or unused long service leave payment".
-- s 10A(1): qualifying earnings are "(a) the person's ordinary time earnings; (b) all commissions payable to the person; (c) all
-- payments for the performance of the person's duties as a member of the executive body ...; (d) all payments under a contract
-- referred to in subsection 12(3) that are in respect of the person's labour under the contract; (e) ... remuneration ... as a
-- member of the Parliament ...; (f) all payments to the person for work referred to in subsection 12(8); (g) all remuneration of
-- the person in circumstances referred to in subsection 12(9) or (10); (h) ... salary sacrifice ... an amount equal to the total
-- of those reductions." (3): "do not include ... (a) a payment ... that represents the reversal of all or part of a sacrificed
-- contribution; (b) earnings ... to the extent that ... of a kind prescribed by the regulations."
--
-- Overtime is in none of the paragraphs: it is neither "ordinary hours of work" nor "over-award payments, shift-loading or
-- commission". Hours worked, and the worker's age, appear nowhere in s 10A.
DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `earnings for ordinary hours`
    `an over-award payment`
    `a shift loading`
    `a commission`
    `overtime`
    `a termination lump sum in lieu of unused sick leave`
    `a termination lump sum for unused annual or long service leave`
    `director's fees`
    `the labour part of a payment under a s 12(3) contract`
    `the non-labour part of a payment under a s 12(3) contract`
    `remuneration as a member of Parliament`
    `payment for s 12(8) work`
    `remuneration of a public office holder`
    `a salary sacrifice reduction`
    `the reversal of a sacrificed contribution`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of payment`, `excluded by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is qualifying earnings` IF
        (NOT `excluded by the regulations`)
    AND CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `overtime` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a termination lump sum in lieu of unused sick leave` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a termination lump sum for unused annual or long service leave` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `the non-labour part of a payment under a s 12(3) contract` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `the reversal of a sacrificed contribution` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- One pay, broken into its parts; the parts that are qualifying earnings are added (s 10A(2): an amount is "counted only once").
DECLARE Pay HAS
    `ordinary hours pay` IS A NUMBER
    `over-award pay` IS A NUMBER
    `shift loading pay` IS A NUMBER
    `commission pay` IS A NUMBER
    `overtime pay` IS A NUMBER
    `termination leave lump sums` IS A NUMBER
    `salary sacrificed` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the pay` IS A Pay
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the qualifying earnings in the pay` MEANS
        `the pay`'s `ordinary hours pay`
    PLUS `the pay`'s `over-award pay`
    PLUS `the pay`'s `shift loading pay`
    PLUS `the pay`'s `commission pay`
    PLUS `the pay`'s `salary sacrificed`

§§ `s 10A(6) and s 17B -- the maximum contributions base as a cap`

-- s 10A(6): if a payment "results in the employee's total qualifying earnings: (a) during the financial year; and (b) in relation
-- to the employer; exceeding the maximum contributions base, then treat the amount of that payment as if it were equal to: (c) if
-- that payment caused that total to exceed that base--so much of that payment as does not include the excess; or (d) if an earlier
-- payment had already caused that total to exceed that base--nil."
-- s 17B: if an employer shortfall exemption certificate is in force for the employer and a period including the QE day, "treat
-- the employee as having already reached the maximum contributions base before the QE day."
-- The base itself is worked out by a formula in s 10A(5) that is not in the deposit: an INPUT.
GIVEN `earlier qualifying earnings this year from the employer` IS A NUMBER, `the payment` IS A NUMBER,
      `the maximum contributions base` IS A NUMBER, `an exemption certificate is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment as counted` MEANS
    IF `an exemption certificate is in force` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `earlier qualifying earnings this year from the employer` AT LEAST `the maximum contributions base` THEN 0
         ELSE `the lesser of` `the payment`
                              (`the maximum contributions base` MINUS `earlier qualifying earnings this year from the employer`)

§§ `s 17A -- the individual superannuation guarantee amount`

-- s 17A(1): "This Subdivision applies if an employer makes a payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee on a particular
-- day (the QE day)." (2): "On the QE day, the employer has an individual superannuation guarantee amount for the employee equal
-- to: [formula not in the deposit] where: amount of the qualifying earnings means: (a) if there is one such payment--the amount of
-- the payment; or (b) if there are 2 or more such payments--the sum of the amounts of the payments. ... charge percentage means 12."
-- INFERENCE: the formula is the amount times the charge percentage over 100 (s 17: "a particular percentage of the payment").
-- The text sets one figure, 12, with no date table.
`the charge percentage` MEANS 12

GIVEN `the amount of the qualifying earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the individual superannuation guarantee amount` MEANS
    `the amount of the qualifying earnings` TIMES `the charge percentage` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `s 6(1) -- business days, the usual period and the extended usual period`

-- s 6(1): "business day means a day other than: (a) a Saturday or a Sunday; or (b) a day which is a public holiday for the whole
-- of: (i) any State; or (ii) the Australian Capital Territory; or (iii) the Northern Territory." "usual period, for a QE day ...
-- (a) starting on the QE day; and (b) ending on the seventh business day after the QE day." "extended usual period ... ending on
-- the 20th business day after the QE day."
-- Public holidays are not in the Act: an INPUT list of YYYYMMDD dates. A holiday in one State alone is enough.
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole part of` MEANS TRUNC `x` 0

GIVEN `ymd` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of` MEANS `the whole part of` (`ymd` DIVIDED BY 10000)

GIVEN `ymd` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month of` MEANS `the whole part of` (`ymd` DIVIDED BY 100) MINUS (`the year of` `ymd`) TIMES 100

GIVEN `ymd` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day of the month of` MEANS `ymd` MINUS (`the whole part of` (`ymd` DIVIDED BY 100)) TIMES 100

-- Days since 1 January 1970 (a civil-calendar count; arithmetic only, not law).
GIVEN `ymd` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the March-based year of` MEANS
    IF `the month of` `ymd` AT MOST 2 THEN `the year of` `ymd` MINUS 1 ELSE `the year of` `ymd`

GIVEN `ymd` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the March-based month of` MEANS
    IF `the month of` `ymd` GREATER THAN 2 THEN `the month of` `ymd` MINUS 3 ELSE `the month of` `ymd` PLUS 9

GIVEN `ymd` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day of the March-based year of` MEANS
    (`the whole part of` ((`the March-based month of` `ymd` TIMES 153 PLUS 2) DIVIDED BY 5))
    PLUS `the day of the month of` `ymd` MINUS 1

GIVEN `ymd` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day count of` MEANS
        `era` TIMES 146097
        PLUS `yoe` TIMES 365 PLUS `the whole part of` (`yoe` DIVIDED BY 4) MINUS `the whole part of` (`yoe` DIVIDED BY 100)
        PLUS `the day of the March-based year of` `ymd`
        MINUS 719468
    WHERE
        `y` MEANS `the March-based year of` `ymd`
        `era` MEANS `the whole part of` (`y` DIVIDED BY 400)
        `yoe` MEANS `y` MINUS `era` TIMES 400

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a listed holiday` MEANS
    CONSIDER `holidays`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `h` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN `the day count of` `h` EQUALS `n` OR `is a listed holiday` `n` `rest`

-- 1 January 1970 was a Thursday, so the count plus 4, modulo 7, is 0 on a Sunday and 6 on a Saturday.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a business day` IF
        (`n` PLUS 4) MODULO 7 GREATER THAN 0
    AND (`n` PLUS 4) MODULO 7 LESS THAN 6
    AND (NOT (`is a listed holiday` `n` `holidays`))

GIVEN `from` IS A NUMBER
      `count` IS A NUMBER
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the business day after` MEANS
    IF `count` EQUALS 0 THEN `from`
    ELSE IF `is a business day` (`from` PLUS 1) `holidays`
         THEN `the business day after` (`from` PLUS 1) (`count` MINUS 1) `holidays`
         ELSE `the business day after` (`from` PLUS 1) `count` `holidays`

GIVEN `the QE day` IS A NUMBER
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of the usual period` MEANS
    `the business day after` (`the day count of` `the QE day`) 7 `holidays`

GIVEN `the QE day` IS A NUMBER
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of the extended usual period` MEANS
    `the business day after` (`the day count of` `the QE day`) 20 `holidays`

§§ `s 18C(1), (2) item 1 -- when an eligible contribution counts for the QE day`

-- s 18C(1)(c): the contribution must be "received during one of these periods (the standard periods): (i) the usual period for
-- the current QE day; or (ii) the 12-month period ending on the day before the current QE day; or before the end of the latest day
-- in any applicable items of the table in subsection (2)". (2) item 1: if "the eligible contribution is the first eligible
-- contribution made to a particular complying superannuation fund or RSA by the employer for the benefit of the employee: (a)
-- after the employee commenced (or recommenced) employment with the employer; or (b) after the employer ceased making ... eligible
-- contributions ... to another complying superannuation fund or RSA", it may be received "during the extended usual period".
GIVEN `the QE day` IS A NUMBER
      `received on` IS A NUMBER
      `the first contribution to this fund after starting or switching` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contribution is received in time for the QE day` IF
        `received on` AT LEAST `the QE day` MINUS 10000
    AND (    `the day count of` `received on` AT MOST `the last day of the usual period` `the QE day` `holidays`
         OR  (    `the first contribution to this fund after starting or switching`
              AND `the day count of` `received on` AT MOST `the last day of the extended usual period` `the QE day` `holidays`))

§§ `ss 18C, 18D -- the individual base and final shortfalls`

-- s 18C(1): "An employer's individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall for an employee and a QE day is equal to: [formula
-- not in the deposit] where: eligible contributions relevant for the QE day means so much of each eligible contribution ... as ...
-- (d) does not cause the amount resulting from this subsection ... to be less than nil."
-- s 18D(1): the final shortfall is "(a) if the employer's individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall ... is nil--nil; or
-- (b) otherwise--equal to the amount in subsection (2)"; (2) [formula not in the deposit] counts contributions "received during
-- the late period", again so as not to go below nil. "late period" (s 6(1)) runs from the day after the last day a contribution
-- could count under s 18C(1) to the day before the assessment.
-- INFERENCE: each formula is the earlier amount less the contributions it names, not below nil.
GIVEN `the individual superannuation guarantee amount for the day` IS A NUMBER, `eligible contributions received in time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the individual base shortfall` MEANS
    `not below nil` (`the individual superannuation guarantee amount for the day` MINUS `eligible contributions received in time`)

GIVEN `the base shortfall` IS A NUMBER, `eligible contributions received in the late period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the individual final shortfall` MEANS
    IF `the base shortfall` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `not below nil` (`the base shortfall` MINUS `eligible contributions received in the late period`)

§§ `s 19B -- the administrative uplift`

-- s 19 applies "if an employer has an individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall for an employee and a QE day that is
-- greater than nil". s 19B(1): "The employer's administrative uplift amount for the QE day is equal to 60% of the sum of: (a) the
-- total of the employer's individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for the QE day; and (b) the total of the employer's
-- individual notional earnings components for the QE day." (2): "this amount may be reduced (but not below nil) in accordance
-- with the regulations" -- not encoded. The notional earnings component (s 19A) uses a formula not in the deposit: an INPUT.
GIVEN `total final shortfalls` IS A NUMBER, `total notional earnings components` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the administrative uplift amount` MEANS
    60 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES (`total final shortfalls` PLUS `total notional earnings components`)

§§ `ss 20A, 20C, 20D -- the choice loading`

-- s 20A(1): the choice loading is "(a) if subsection (2) or (3) applies to some or all of those eligible contributions--the lower
-- of: (i) the amount equal to 25% of the total of the contributions to which that subsection applies; and (ii) the choice loading
-- limit for the QE day; or (b) otherwise--nil." (2) applies to contributions "not made in compliance with the choice of fund
-- requirements" where "(b) section 20D (relying on most recent Commissioner notification) does not apply".
-- s 20C(1): "The choice loading limit for the QE day ... is $1,200." (2): "reduced (but not below nil) by the amount equal to 25%
-- of the sum of any other eligible contributions" to which s 20A(2) or (3) applied "for any earlier QE day ... during the notice
-- period", which (3) begins no earlier than "1 July 2026".
GIVEN `earlier non-complying contributions in the notice period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the choice loading limit` MEANS
    `not below nil` (1200 MINUS 25 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `earlier non-complying contributions in the notice period`)

GIVEN `non-complying contributions for the QE day` IS A NUMBER, `earlier non-complying contributions in the notice period` IS A NUMBER,
      `s 20D applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the choice loading` MEANS
    IF `s 20D applies` OR `non-complying contributions for the QE day` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `the lesser of` (25 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `non-complying contributions for the QE day`)
                         (`the choice loading limit` `earlier non-complying contributions in the notice period`)

§§ `s 16B -- the superannuation guarantee shortfall`

-- s 16B(1): applies if the employer has "(a) one or more individual base superannuation guarantee shortfalls for a QE day that are
-- greater than nil; or (b) one or more choice loadings for a QE day that are greater than nil." (2): the shortfall is "the sum of
-- ... (a) the total of the employer's individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls ...; (b) the total of the employer's
-- individual notional earnings components ...; (c) the employer's administrative uplift amount ...; (d) the total of the
-- employer's choice loadings". s 16A: the charge "is payable by the employer".
GIVEN `total base shortfalls` IS A NUMBER, `total final shortfalls` IS A NUMBER, `total notional earnings components` IS A NUMBER,
      `total choice loadings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the superannuation guarantee shortfall` MEANS
    IF `total base shortfalls` GREATER THAN 0 OR `total choice loadings` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN     `total final shortfalls`
        PLUS `total notional earnings components`
        PLUS (IF `total base shortfalls` GREATER THAN 0
              THEN `the administrative uplift amount` `total final shortfalls` `total notional earnings components`
              ELSE 0)
        PLUS `total choice loadings`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 32C, 32CA -- where the contribution must go`

-- s 32C(1): compliant if made to "(a) a chosen fund for the employee". (1A): compliant if "(a) there is no chosen fund for the
-- employee; and (b) the most recent notification to the employer ... by the Commissioner ... is that the Commissioner is satisfied
-- that the fund is the stapled fund for the employee." (1B): (1A) does not apply if the employer was required under s 32N to give
-- a standard choice form and has not done so in time. (2): compliant if there is no chosen fund, the Commissioner's most recent
-- notification is "that there is no stapled fund for the employee", "(b) the fund is an eligible choice fund", "(ba)" it is the
-- fund named in the standard choice form, "(c) a class of beneficial interest in the fund is a MySuper product", and (d), (e)
-- death-benefit requirements in the regulations (an INPUT folded into the MySuper flag). (2A): (2) likewise does not apply while
-- a standard choice form is overdue. s 32CA: "Despite section 32C", not compliant "if the employer imposes a direct cost or charge
-- on the employee as a consequence of having to contribute to that fund."
-- The order is the Act's: the employee's chosen fund; failing that, the stapled fund the Commissioner names; failing that, the
-- employer's default fund with a MySuper product. Other routes in s 32C(1)(b), (2AB)-(9) are not encoded.
DECLARE `Fund facts` HAS
    `there is a chosen fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid to the chosen fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner named this fund as the stapled fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner notified there is no stapled fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid to the default fund named in the standard choice form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the default fund is an eligible choice fund with a MySuper product meeting the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a standard choice form is overdue` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer imposes a direct cost for the fund` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the fund facts` IS A `Fund facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contribution complies with the choice of fund requirements` IF
        (NOT (`the fund facts`'s `the employer imposes a direct cost for the fund`))
    AND (    (`the fund facts`'s `there is a chosen fund` AND `the fund facts`'s `paid to the chosen fund`)
         OR  (    (NOT (`the fund facts`'s `there is a chosen fund`))
              AND (NOT (`the fund facts`'s `a standard choice form is overdue`))
              AND (    `the fund facts`'s `the Commissioner named this fund as the stapled fund`
                   OR  (    `the fund facts`'s `the Commissioner notified there is no stapled fund`
                        AND `the fund facts`'s `paid to the default fund named in the standard choice form`
                        AND `the fund facts`'s `the default fund is an eligible choice fund with a MySuper product meeting the regulations`))))
